# Ignore mobile app — it's a separate Expo project built via EAS, not Vercel
mobile/
mobile/node_modules/
mobile/.expo/
mobile/android/
mobile/ios/
mobile/dist/
mobile/web-build/

# Ignore tests — they parity-pin against mobile/ (stripped above), so next build's
# type-check cannot resolve their ../../mobile imports in the Vercel upload
# (W4-W9 production deploys 5e74620f..7ebf6a9f all ERRORed on TS2307 —
# family pattern: SmartBot's .vercelignore strips tests too).
# CI still runs the full tree: npm run typecheck + test:coverage + build.
tests/
tests/e2e/

# Ignore e2e specs (Maestro/Playwright artifacts — never needed at runtime)
maestro/

# Ignore WebToMobile plugin docs/skills (not needed in deployment)
docs/web-to-mobile/
docs/mobile-progress.md
docs/mobile-final-report.md

# Ignore AI/tooling
.agents/
.claude/
claude.md
